  "text_sanskrit": "युक्ताहारविहारस्य युक्तचेष्टस्य कर्मसु । युक्तस्वप्नावबोधस्य योगो भवति दुःखहा ॥ ६-१७ ॥",
  "itrans": "yuktAhAravihArasya yuktacheShTasya karmasu . yuktasvapnAvabodhasya yogo bhavati duHkhahA .. 6-17 ..",
  "translation": "Of him whose food and exercise are of due measure, whose labour in matters of duty is regulated, whose sleep and wakefulness are also regulated, of him the Yoga becomes capable of killing out misery (17)\nV. In 16 the prohibition regarding food and vigils refers to persons who are naturally weak. In the case of those who are endowed with powers of endurance and absolute abstinence wakefulness, &c., cannot interfere with the course of meditation.\nVerse 17 states the positive conditions promoting the Yoga practice and its effects. (16-17) \nA. The Yoga when accomplished is observed to be as follows.",
